ch is corroborated by [P13] and [P16], but the figure of 50% allocation to each fund is not directly matched in any evidence; the nearest comparable is the FE scatter label showing a blended 'Risk 7' portfolio but no discrete 50/50 split is stated."],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["No explicit SRRI risk rating of 7 disclosed for Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity in the case file; the available SRRI rating from the fund's own KIID is 4, not 7.","No direct confirmation of the 0.20% ongoing charge figure for Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity in any retrieved passage.","The report does not disclose the basis or scale upon which the stated fund-level risk ratings of 7 are assigned (e.g., whether they are SRRI, FE, or proprietary firm ratings), making it unclear whether a risk rating of 7 on one scale is comparable to the client's agreed rating of 7."],"analysis":"The core discrepancy is material: the Vanguard LifeStrategy 80% Equity fund's own regulatory SRRI disclosure ([P13]) states a risk rating of 4, not 7. The report asserts both funds carry a risk rating of 7 to match the client's agreed risk profile. This is contradicted by the Vanguard fund's own KIID. The guard states that 'Fund-level risk ratings from a provider are not necessarily on the firm's client risk scale,' and indeed the Vanguard SRRI (4) and the report's stated rating (7) are on different scales — SRRI being regulatory (1–7 ordinal) and the report's claim of 7 appearing to be on an internal or commercial scale (possibly FE Analytics' scale, which is corroborated for the blended portfolio in [P14]). However, the report nowhere discloses that these are different scales, nor does it explain the relationship between the fund's SRRI rating of 4 and the assigned rating of 7. The FE scatter chart ([P14]) does label the combined portfolio 'Risk 7,' confirming that on some scale the blended strategy is positioned at risk 7. This suggests the report may be using a 0–10 commercial scale where 7 is appropriate for a portfolio holding 80% equity, whereas the fund's SRRI is the regulatory 1–7 scale where 4 reflects a balanced multi-asset profile. The two are not contradictory in outcome (a 4 on SRRI can be consistent with a 7 on a commercial scale for a blended portfolio), but the failure to disclose that the fund's disclosed risk rating (4) differs materially from the claimed match (7) is a significant transparency gap. It leaves unresolved whether the client has been informed that one of the two recommended funds carries a regulatory risk rating (4) that is substantially lower than the stated target (7). The 0.20% ongoing charge for Vanguard is not corroborated in the evidence; no passage confirms this figure. The 50% allocation split is stated in the report but not independently verified in any retrieved passage, though the blended portfolio as a whole is referenced in [P14]. The discrepancy in the Vanguard ongoing charge figure (0.20% stated in report vs. no confirmation in evidence) and the absence of a disclosed scale reconciliation for the risk ratings constitute material gaps in justification.","citations":[{"passageId":"P13","source":"Vanguard & HSBC KIIDS.md","category":"H","quote":"The Fund is rated 4 due to the nature of its investments which include the risks listed below.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Vanguard & HSBC KIIDS.md","category":"H","quote":"Ongoing charge | it 0.19%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P16","source":"Vanguard & HSBC fact sheets.md","category":"H","quote":"Ongoing charge figure² | 0.190%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"FE scatter chart for reprot.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Risk 7 HSBC Gl Dyn/Vanguard LS 80 TR in GB","59.29","8.63"]},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Vanguard& HSBC KIIDS.md","category":"H","quote":"The Fund is rated 4 due to the nature of its investments which include the risks listed below. These factors may impact the value of the Fund's investments or expose the Fund to losses.",