#### Contradictions the extraction found in the report, on your paths
These were recorded when the report was read in full. They are the report disagreeing with itself, not a document disagreeing with the report, so no passage is needed to establish them and no guard about differing sources explains them.

- Client objectives state desire to retire at 60 with annual income of £25,000–£30,000 and explicit preference for 'flexible income over guaranteed income'. Risk profile is assessed as 7/10 (Growth). Cashflow analysis shows assets would be sufficient even in stress scenarios including 6% inflation and 2007/8-style market crash. However, the incompatibility between a growth-oriented risk profile and the relatively modest income target (£25k–£30k on projected assets) is not explicitly addressed; the high risk profile appears suited to capital accumulation rather than the stated income objectives.
