## Nest growth funds
The following funds have been designed for members who haven't yet reached State Pension age. They're designed to target a range of growth objectives and take different levels of investment risk to achieve this.
Introduction Underlying funds Key metrics Nest retirement funds Nest growth funds
## Nest 2040 Retirement Fund
(default strategy - growth phase)
## Default strategy
Nest's flagship default strategy provides a fund for each year in which we expect a member could retire. We manage members' assets according to their age and how markets are performing. If members join in their early twenties they'll go through four, dynamically managed investment phases. Most members will spend most of their time invested in the growth phase. It's the engine room of the default strategy, aiming to grow well above inflation over 30 years. The consolidation phase prepares members' money as they approach retirement. The Nest 2040 Retirement Fund is in the growth phase of this lifecycle.
## Investment performance
## Fund objectives
target investment returns equivalent to CPI plus 3% and cover all scheme charges over the long term
expect a long-term volatility average of 11%
aim for steady growth in real terms over the life of the fund
maximise retirement incomes by taking sufficient investment risk at appropriate times while reducing the likelihood of extreme investment shocks
