These policies operate on the 'Money Purchase' basis (also known as 'Defined Contribution') & provide a fund of money, at retirement, which is then used to purchase a pension and normally a Pension Commencement Lump Sum (PCLS).   The amount of the fund at retirement is dependent upon the level of contributions paid, the investment return on the contributions once invested, and the charges under the policy.
At retirement the fund can be used to provide a pension by purchasing an annuity in the open market (guaranteed income), the amount of pension provided is therefore dependent upon the annuity rates then available in the market or by entering Drawdown. The income from a drawdown contract is not guaranteed and will depend on future investment returns and levels of withdrawals.
