erence at each growth rate depending on whether existing adviser charges are included","Quilter comparison states existing 0.27% versus recommended 0.19%, marked 'Better', but the comparison is conditional ('If you were to retain...'); no actual existing arrangement details for Quilter fund range or retirement options appear in the report's comparison section","True Potential comparison presents existing charges as 0.40% + 0.50% + 0.58% = 1.48% in the text, but replacement analysis uses 0.98%, a discrepancy of 0.50% (the ongoing advice charge) not explained in the comparison logic","Report comparison table shows True Potential Risk Alignment as N/A or unmarked, but no dimension comparison addresses why True Potential's existing funds were suitable at acquisition and are now being switched for risk reasons (only addressed for Nest)","Nest existing retirement options stated as 'Full and partial UFPLS only (Flexi-access drawdown not available)' versus recommended 'Flexi-access drawdown, full and partial UFPLS', but Aviva KFD [P10] confirms both options are available at Aviva; the distinction of 'benefit' depends on whether Nest genuinely lacks flexi-access drawdown","Report presents multiple SAP scenarios with different charge bases but provides no explanation of which scenario applies to the recommendation or why three different RIY figures (1.5%, 0.5%, 0.4%) represent the same recommendation"],"comparisonPerformed":true,"missingInputs":["Nest scheme documentation confirming whether flexi-access drawdown is genuinely unavailable in existing scheme or whether it is available","Historical performance comparison of True Potential's existing holdings versus Aviva's proposed fund allocation to substantiate any performance-based switching rationale","Safeguarded benefits, guarantees, or valuable features of existing arrangements that may be lost on transfer","Details of any alternative recommendations considered (investment pathways are dismissed but no other platforms or solutions are compared)","Explicit statement of which SAP charge scenario ('All charges inc', 'All charges ex', 'IAC only') represents the basis of the recommendation","Explanation of the basis for assessing True Potential charges as 'Better' when fund projections show -12.42% reduction at all growth rates","Documentation of any employer contributions in Nest or True Potential schemes that may be forfeited","Confirmation of fund range availability: True Potential stated as 35 funds, but only six are shown in the replacement analysis comparison"],"analysis":"The comparison dimension on Charges for True Potential contains an internal logic error. The report states existing 0.98% versus recommended 0.39%, which is a reduction of 0.59 percentage points and should be marked 'Better' for cost grounds. However, the projected fund values at retirement show a -12.42% reduction across all growth scenarios when moved to Aviva, contradicting the cost advantage. This suggests either (a) the charges comparison is on a different basis than the projections, (b) performance differs between the funds in a way that offsets the cost saving, or (c) the comparison mixes inclusive and exclusive charge bases. The extraction flagged internal inconsistency: True Potential charges in the existing arrangements table are listed as 0.40% + 0.50% + 0.58% = 1.48%, but the replacement analysis uses 0.98%, which equals 0.40% + 0.58% only (excluding the 0.50% ongoing advice charge). This suggests the comparison may be excluding ongoing adviser services, yet the report recommends ongoing servicing with Aviva at 0.39% (platform 0.19% + investment 0.20%). If the 0.39% includes servicing, it is not directly comparable to 0.98% excluding it. No explanation of these bases is provided in the report. For Nest, the comparison lists existing charges as 0.30% + 1.8% but the SAP analysis calculates impact using 0.30% only, excluding the contribution charge. At £21,272.64 fund value, 1.8% annually equals approximately £382 per year, which is material. The report does not disclose whether this charge applies indefinitely, ceases after initial contributions, or applies only to future contributions; without this, the comparison is incomplete. The SAP charge scenario discrepancy is material: 'All charges inc existing OAC' produces a 1.5% RIY and -12.42% fund reduction, while 'All charges ex existing OAC' produces 0.4% RIY and +12.34% improvement. These cannot both describe the same recommendation. The report provides no statement of which scenario was adopted for the advice. This is a fundamental gap: the recommendation cannot be evaluated against the projections if the charge basis is ambiguous. For Nest, the report states existing retirement options as 'Full and partial UFPLS only (Flexi-access drawdown not available)' versus recommended 'Flexi-access drawdown, full and partial UFPLS' marked 'Better'. Aviva's KFD [P10] confirms flexi-access drawdown is available, but there is no documentation confirming that Nest genuinely lacks this option; if Nest also offers it, the 'Better' assessment for retirement options is incorrect. No safeguarded benefits analysis is provided for any of the three existing schemes. Nest is described as an auto-enrolment workplace pension, which typically carries safeguarded benefits not available in personal pensions; none are mentioned. No alternative options are considered or dismissed with reasoning; investment pathways are rejected (per P1) but no other platforms, consolidation without switching, or retention are discussed. The Quilter comparison is presented as conditional ('If you were to retain...') yet marked as though it is an actual existing holding; the extract states 0.27% charges but notes in [I] passage that this is hypothetical wording, creating ambiguity about whether Quilter is a current holding or a comparison baseline. The report does not address why Quilter (if held) is being replaced or what features it offers relative to Aviva. Overall, the comparison framework shows multiple inconsistencies in charge bases, contradictions between cost assessments and fund projections, missing documentation of existing scheme features (safeguards, retirement options confirmation, contribution arrangements), and no documented alternative analysis. These gaps prevent full verification of consistency between the recommendation and supporting evidence.","citations":[{"passageId":"P18","source":"Annes M SAP All charges inc existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Existing Schemes*: £48,408 / £121,807 / £298,632; Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice): £42,300 / £106,000 / £261,000; The effect this will have on the fund if moved to Aviva: -12.42% / -12.42% / -12.42%; Reduction in Yield if moved to Aviva: 1.5% / 1.5% / 1.6%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P14","source":"Annes M SAP no charges ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Existing Schemes*: £53,497 / £134,612 / £330,027; Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice): £60,100 / £151,000 / £370,000; The effect this will have on the fund if moved to Aviva: +12.34% / +12.34% / +12.34%; Reduction in Yield if moved to Aviva: 0.4%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P15","source":"Annes M SAP IAC only ex existing OAC 24.3.26.md","category":"G","quote":"Aviva Pension Portfolio (Choice): £58,200 / £146,000 / £359,000; Reduction in Yield if moved to Aviva: 0.5%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"It has not performed as well as the recommended investment strategy. Why are investment pathways not appropriate for you? I have considered the investment pathway solution offered by the recommended provider...However, I have discounted it because...It has not performed as well as the recommended investment strategy.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Aviva Pension KFD.md","category":"G","quote":"Flexi-access drawdown, you can also take one-off withdrawals either alongside or instead of regular withdrawals...you h